# Project health

Measured from the database, following the [CHAOSS](https://chaoss.community) metrics for project health: responsiveness (time to first response, change request
closure ratio), contributor sustainability (contributor absence factor) and release frequency. **Bots are excluded from every response number.** These figures describe
activity. They cannot tell a busy maintainer from one who has stepped back, and they say nothing about quality; read them next to the [register](register.md).
Only aggregates are shown: no person other than the configured maintainers is singled out.

## Who is talking

Comments on issues and pull requests (including code-review comments), per year.

{% if activity %}
| Year | By maintainers | By everyone else | Maintainer share |
|---|---|---|---|
{% for r in activity %}
| {{ r.year }} | {{ r.by_maintainers }} | {{ r.by_others }} | {{ ((100 * r.by_maintainers) / (r.by_maintainers + r.by_others)) | round(0) | int if (r.by_maintainers + r.by_others) else 0 }}% |
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
No comment data yet (run `fi acquire`).
{% endif %}

## Responsiveness: time to first response

Days until a human other than the author first commented on an issue, per year the issue was opened. "No response" counts issues that never got one.

{% if unanswered %}
| Year opened | Issues | Median days to first response | No response | Share with none |
|---|---|---|---|---|
{% for u in unanswered %}
{% set d = ttfr | selectattr('year', 'equalto', u.year) | map(attribute='days') | sort | list %}
| {{ u.year }} | {{ u.issues }} | {{ d[(d | length) // 2] if d else '-' }} | {{ u.no_response }} | {{ ((100 * u.no_response) / u.issues) | round(0) | int }}% |
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
No data.
{% endif %}

## Change request closure

Pull requests opened and closed (merged or declined) per year. A ratio below 100% means the backlog of pull requests grew.

{% if pr_opened %}
| Year | Opened | Closed | Merged | Closure ratio |
|---|---|---|---|---|
{% for o in pr_opened %}
{% set c = pr_closed | selectattr('year', 'equalto', o.year) | list %}
| {{ o.year }} | {{ o.opened }} | {{ c[0].closed if c else 0 }} | {{ c[0].merged if c else 0 }} | {{ ((100 * (c[0].closed if c else 0)) / o.opened) | round(0) | int }}% |
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
No pull requests.
{% endif %}

## Contributor sustainability: contributor absence factor

The smallest number of people who made at least half of the commits in the year (formerly "bus factor"). 1 means one person carries the project.

{% if commits %}
| Year | Commits | Contributors | Absence factor |
|---|---|---|---|
{% for year, rows in commits | groupby('year') %}
{% set total = rows | sum(attribute='n') %}
{% set ns = namespace(acc=0, k=0) %}
{% for r in rows %}{% if ns.acc * 2 < total %}{% set ns.acc = ns.acc + r.n %}{% set ns.k = ns.k + 1 %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
| {{ year }} | {{ total }} | {{ rows | length }} | {{ ns.k }} |
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
No commits acquired.
{% endif %}

